# Insidious Roots: "Creature tokens you control have '{T}: Add one mana of any color.'" Bot1 has Roots, a nontoken Ornithopter and two
# Goblin tokens (Dragon Fodder). The tokens are summoning sick on turn 1 (the granted ability has {T} in its cost, CR 302.6), so it is
# refused; the nontoken Ornithopter never has it. Bot2 makes its own Goblin tokens with its Dragon Fodder: Roots gives them nothing.
# On turn 3 a Goblin token taps for {U} (a mana ability, no stack) and pays Ancestral Recall, which draws three.

[Bot1 Deck]
Insidious Roots
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Dragon Fodder
Ornithopter
Ancestral Recall
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Dragon Fodder
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Insidious Roots.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dragon Fodder.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token#1.Activate(Color: Blue)
! Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Activate(Color: Blue)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Dragon Fodder.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token#1.Activate(Color: Blue)
? Bot1.Mana = {U}
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
! Bot2.Battlefield.Goblin Token#1.Activate(Color: Blue)

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token#2.Tapped = false
Bot1.Graveyard = Ancestral Recall; Dragon Fodder
